Z||000000||Wrench||10-05-1999||08:44 PM||||When I pull the pulgs on my '86 GT they are white! I get about 30mpg and drive 60 miles each way to work, all at 70+mph. Also I do not hear the fuel pump "whine" anymore when I turn the key to the first detent. Car starts, stalls and then on the second start manages to stay alive. Currently at 130K miles. Should I be concerned about possible lean burn? Car runs fine at highway speeds.||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||10-05-1999||10:36 PM||||A beige or slightly grey color is indicative of normal operation and is easy to mistake for "white".  You would probably have some obvious problems related to lean mixture (ie.. red hot exh. manifolds)if this were actually the case.  <BR>     The fuel pump problem is more than likely related to your oil pressure sender than the pump itself (if it runs at all).  <P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
